  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening farmers&apos; food security in the first communal section of Anse-Rouge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Most small-scale farmers in Haiti&apos;s l&apos;Artibonite department lack the resources to produce sufficient food or earn enough income to support their families. The IAF supports community-led solutions to expand economic opportunities through sustainable agriculture and micro-enterprise development. Our grantee Association des Cadres et Agriculteurs pour le Dveloppement d&apos;une Agriculture Innove et Intgre dans l&apos;Artibonite (ACADAI) is improving economic resilience and food security by protecting the environment, increasing farmers&apos; access to seeds and livestock and by strengthening small businesses through access to credit. This grant advances the IAF&apos;s strategic initiative to promote sustainable agriculture by strengthening food security efforts and supporting viable livelihoods.</narrative>
  </description>
